##############################################################################
# PolyKernel Todo 10 (Wave 2): CUDA MatMul + Softmax kernels + CPU reference — QA log
# Extends the Todo 8/9 framework (RMSNorm/GELU/SiLU). Deliverables: matmul.cu
# (tiled shared-mem GEMM, fp32 accum, NO tensor cores) + softmax.cu (stable, one
# block/row) CUDA kernels (portable template), --lower-to-cuda matmul/softmax
# emitters (byte-identical to standalone), launch_matmul_cpu + launch_softmax_cpu
# CPU refs + drivers, CPU-ref-vs-golden tests. RMSNorm/GELU/SiLU re-confirmed.
# ROUNDING CONTRACT: bf16 (RNE) in, fp32 compute/accumulate, bf16 out (golden.py).
# MatMul C[M,N]=A[M,K]@B[K,N] (batched leading dims flattened into M, np.matmul).
# Softmax: stable (subtract row max before exp), last axis, fp32, bf16 out.
##############################################################################

